<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell 12 points to 1,481.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell 12 points to 1,481.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,481 today from 1,493 on April 2, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.  Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1484    13.475	  1497    13.594</p>
<p>   1a   1489 11275.000	  1510 11438.000</p>
<p>   2    1787    25.531	  1808    25.831</p>
<p>   2a   1834 15044.000	  1852 15188.000</p>
<p>   3    1738    16.038	  1732    15.981</p>
<p>   3a   1557 12288.000	  1572 12406.000</p>
<p>   6    1238    12.769	  1239    12.775</p>
